# Defines key English terms that should be used consistently in the application,
# such that translators can define standard equivalents in their language,
# which Weblate will suggest when translating strings which include those terms.
#
# GNU gettext Portable Object syntax:
#   #. Definition of the term, visible to translators when the term is matched by Weblate.
#   #, Term-specific flags, including:
#      read-only: term should not be translated.
#      terminology: all languages should provide an equivalent (implicit by Weblate configuration).
#   msgid "term"
#     Translation key for the term, usually the same as the term, but:
#     - If ambiguous, prefix by some context and a dot.
#     - If it could be a noun or a verb, suffix with .noun / .verb
#   msgstr "term"
#     The English term
#
# Also include English variants like plurals, past tense, gerund, so Weblate matches them all.

